rogress on server-2 GPU0; after terminal validation compare ScanRefer mIoU and fixed-protocol efficiency with B4-E30, without validation tuning.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/admissions/AdaRES-G1.json\", \"sha256\": \"5de6b4715e2f602bce22a771518b26db138fcaadaa23c8b59fe3de7ea1b155d5\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-G1-H5_launch_verification_20260925-173300.md\", \"sha256\": \"1d76b8a60764e8d0889a2c9bd4bdff5eb9790fd5dda9b0468825eec510bf575e\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-H1\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"No sampler-omission candidate; reconsider only with independent evidence that available target-bearing seeds are systematically dropped.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-H1_sampling_16scenes_20260925.json\", \"sha256\": \"cc1cc87133c3cc72779054f32f12656add6e0b1aef19c63787ef2d4e793b0bca\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-H1-H4_negative_diagnoses_20260925-173300.md\", \"sha256\": \"99bc3de0321dc060eaff1a86cf6a365004bfd75bb7fc2b16c9e002fe6f21ffbd\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-H2\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"Do not implement four-per-query first-layer shortlist; fixed coverage was slightly lower than B4. No validation top-k scan.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-H2_fine_16scenes_20260925.json\", \"sha256\": \"4f9bdadf802532e6ff233fa3c9cf6eee2921524fa399f0cded4b90a7d9b56fea\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-H1-H4_negative_diagnoses_20260925-173300.md\", \"sha256\": \"99bc3de0321dc060eaff1a86cf6a365004bfd75bb7fc2b16c9e002fe6f21ffbd\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-H3\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"Do not use B4's score head as a standalone selector or scan score fusion weights on validation.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-H3_score_16scenes_20260925.json\", \"sha256\": \"647dc6a532ce04d524ef278b985f817d43b20aefd369a3eba4d5fbd279a4115c\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-H1-H4_negative_diagnoses_20260925-173300.md\", \"sha256\": \"99bc3de0321dc060eaff1a86cf6a365004bfd75bb7fc2b16c9e002fe6f21ffbd\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-H4\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"Do not introduce a simple relation-gated indicator; relation-marked expressions were not enriched among errors in the fixed cohort.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-H4_relation_16scenes_20260925.json\", \"sha256\": \"096c4e213d57394ae1696ab786f8f0ad5c375cf0b7142ec0617d9a4dbfbe5785\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-H1-H4_negative_diagnoses_20260925-173300.md\", \"sha256\": \"99bc3de0321dc060eaff1a86cf6a365004bfd75bb7fc2b16c9e002fe6f21ffbd\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-H5\",\n      \"stage\": \"closed\",\n      \"experiment_id\": \"AdaRES-H5\",\n      \"next_action\": \"Closed at best mIoU 0.5061 after 30 validations and protected early stop, 0.0033 below B4-E30. Do not tune or relaunch late all-query attention; auxiliary terminal metrics remain unavailable.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/admissions/AdaRES-H5.json\", \"sha256\": \"2adbef0bb83e27bb7120ae19a56d67465f57f66f8e68d8c3800d02af9a67b0df\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-G1-H5_launch_verification_20260925-173300.md\", \"sha256\": \"1d76b8a60764e8d0889a2c9bd4bdff5eb9790fd5dda9b0468825eec510bf575e\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/experiments/AdaRES-H5.json\", \"sha256\": \"3be2b5ce3a9c438eaa0d7f27f5e5bdc56a2c91b50dee1c0539d64ea5d6b8ae7c\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-H5_done_earlystop_20260926-141100.md\", \"sha256\": \"176783c51a26d09dd7f17a3f82eeed10b130ba4a140d5f3e3f8ff438681909fd\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-J1\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"No training admission. The fixed pooled-language contrast is higher for only 123/240 missed oracle queries, and standalone subset selection mIoU is 0.01315. Reconsider only with a distinct prospective diagnosis, not a validation feature or fusion-weight scan.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-J1-J2_native_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"9997360f5239c9aa8074bc0ad341e8ae6a6c33b23387d195dd5755005a0d0182\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-J1-J2_negative_diagnosis_20260926-141100.md\", \"sha256\": \"648303bdf1c4e976aaa7d847869d03398d016e4cd96d4fcf7dc425cf1c1d4d3b\"},\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_j1_mask_language_evidence.py\", \"sha256\": \"fc152d7b9e99100a521e0ad6040194fa7e652e303a27fd14e0dd276480d725c4\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-J2\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"No training admission. Only 78/240 missed oracles were more overlap-crowded than selected queries. Reconsider only if an independent, predeclared crowding mechanism has new evidence.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-J1-J2_native_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"9997360f5239c9aa8074bc0ad341e8ae6a6c33b23387d195dd5755005a0d0182\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-J1-J2_negative_diagnosis_20260926-141100.md\", \"sha256\": \"648303bdf1c4e976aaa7d847869d03398d016e4cd96d4fcf7dc425cf1c1d4d3b\"}\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"design_cycle\": {\n    \"at\": \"2026-09-26T14:14:17+08:00\",\n    \"candidate_budget\": 1,\n    \"admitted\": 0,\n    \"attempted_ids\": [\"AdaRES-J1\", \"AdaRES-J2\"],\n    \"stop_reason\": \"Two independent executable diagnoses contradicted their proposed mechanisms; earlier bounded routes H1-H4 and E1/F1-F3 are closed. No remaining specifically evidenced executable candidate passes diagnosis this cycle; this is not a claim of global hypothesis exhaustion.\",\n    \"evidence\": [\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-J1-J2_native_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"9997360f5239c9aa8074bc0ad341e8ae6a6c33b23387d195dd5755005a0d0182\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260926-141300.md\", \"sha256\": \"678a264ceed07f13e7ea09f147843a935aa4127a7f1e6188947343b28dca84da\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-141300.md\", \"sha256\": \"2258f9386fd23d8759b1a3ae5d6a48f8eea1379e1a8b49b0ede1fb4293b9639a\"}\n    ],\n    \"resume_condition\": \"When G1 reaches terminal state, compare final metric and error profile to B4-E30; or immediately resume on new independent, testable evidence that specifies a candidate, matched control and next native diagnostic. Never bypass six gates to fill the vacant GPU1.\"\n  },\n  \"migration_notes\": \"AdaRES did not previously have research work tracking; B4 and B5 are the first explicit queued records.\"\n}\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content pipeline/references/autonomous_design.md -Raw; Get-Content pipeline/decisions/20260926-141647_route_change.md -Raw; Get-Content pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-141300.md -Raw; Get-Content pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260926-141300.md -Raw'","aggregated_output":"Get-Content: \r\nLine |\r\n   2 |  Get-Content pipeline/references/autonomous_design.md -Raw; Get-Conten …\r\n     |  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n     | 找不到路径“D:\\project\\AdaRES_project\\pipeline\\references\\autonomous_design.md”，因为该路径不存在。\r\n# AdaRES_project 决策记录\n\n- **时间**: 2026-09-26 14:16:47\n- **类型**: route_change\n- **问题**: H5 terminal at 0.5061; which mechanism can fill GPU1 under six gates?\n- **决策**: Close H5; reject J1 pooled-language contrast and J2 overlap-crowding after fixed native screens; leave GPU1 vacant pending a qualifying mechanism.\n- **依据**: H5 below B4-E30 by 0.0033; J1 oracle contrast higher 123/240, J2 oracle crowding higher 78/240. Neither passes diagnosis.\n- **证据**: pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-H5_done_earlystop_20260926-141100.md; pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-J1-J2_negative_diagnosis_20260926-141100.md; pipeline/research_work.json\n\r\n# Experiment Design - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 14:13 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Motivation\nGoal: \"AdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515.\" Capacity 1/2, admission budget one. This cycle tested whether language contrast or overlap crowding explains B4 selection errors after H5 failed.\n\n## 2. Current Best Results\n| ID | State | mIoU | Acc@0.25 | Acc@0.5 | spmIoU |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| B1 | complete | 0.5020 | 0.610 | 0.553 | 0.467 |\n| B4-E30 | champion | 0.5094 | 0.608 | 0.562 | 0.474 |\n| H5 | early stop after 30 validations | 0.5061 | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable |\n| G1 | training | 0.4983 preflight best | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable |\n\n## 3. Analysis & Direction\nJ1 language contrast is higher for 123/240 missed oracles, with standalone selection mIoU 0.01315 on the fixed subset. J2 missed oracles are more overlap-crowded in 78/240 errors, opposite the suppression hypothesis. Both are observational and insufficient to motivate training. Previous H1-H4 routes were tested and rejected on distinct fixed screens. G1's final outcome may change which bottleneck is worth investigating next.\n\n## 4. Experiment Plan\nNo new experiment admitted. J1/J2 fail diagnosis, so downstream controls, native backward, resource, independence, constraints and receipt gates are not represented as passed. No validation parameter/feature scan, seed repeat, ablation, renamed H5 or B4 duplicate is authorized to fill capacity.\n\n## 5. GPU Allocation Plan\nServer-2 GPU0 remains G1 only. GPU1 is vacant for training; it was used only for read-only native diagnostic inference. Server-6 remains prohibited.\n\n## 6. Implementation Checklist\n- [x] Fixed 16-scene native diagnosis with paired rows and a scene-only control.\n- [x] Reject disconfirmed J1 and J2 hypotheses.\n- [ ] No model/config, admission receipt, sync or queue push until all hard gates pass.\n- [ ] Reassess after G1 terminal metrics or genuinely independent diagnostic evidence.\n\n## 7. Risk Assessment\nFixed-subset probes can overfit conceptual choices even without tuning. Neither negative screen proves that language or competition cannot ever help. No candidate-specific memory/backward evidence exists for J1/J2. H5's full-run auxiliary metrics were not retained by monitor.\n\n## 8. Smell Check\nNo tuning-only candidate was proposed. Selecting a different language pooling rule, overlap definition or mixing weight by validation would be prohibited. Candidate budget is a ceiling, not a reason to bypass diagnosis.\n\nStatus: NO ADMISSION. Design cycle stops after both newly executable distinct mechanisms contradicted their stated diagnoses and prior bounded routes were closed. Resume when G1 terminates or new independent evidence makes a specific route executable.\n\r\n# Motivation Review - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 14:13 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Goal\nAdaRES seeks to improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515. B1 is 0.5020; B4-E30 remains champion at 0.5094, gap 0.0056. All seven goal constraints and three bans remain in force.\n\n## 2. Story Status\n| Hypothesis | Status | Evidence | Gap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Competition-aware confidence | Partial gain | B4-E30 0.5094 | Target not met; historical continuation is not a fresh control |\n| Metric-aligned indicator targets | Training | G1 28/30, best 0.4983 at preflight | Final outcome pending |\n| Late global query communication | Closed | H5 0.5061 after 30 validations, below B4-E30 | No trained gain |\n\n## 3. Experiment Assessment\nH5's native access and backward gates were valid, but its trained result fell 0.0033 below champion. J1 and J2 probed distinct evidence and crowding mechanisms at the fixed B4 checkpoint. Neither paired diagnosis supported its causal direction. Earlier H1-H4, E1, F1-F3 diagnoses were negative; D1, F4, B3, B5 and C1/C2 training did not beat B4-E30.\n\n## 4. Gap Analysis\nThere is substantial bounded oracle-mask headroom (0.87316 versus 0.49186 selected subset mIoU), but prior standalone signals and altered information paths have not reliably turned it into generalizing confidence. G1 remains the only active test. Full-run active-query, latency and peak-memory measurements remain missing for H5.\n\n## 5. Design Rationale\nJ1 tested language-matched foreground-minus-background scene evidence. Oracle contrast exceeded selected in 123/240 errors, near an even split. J2 tested overlap crowding; only 78/240 missed oracles were more crowded. Neither proceeds to a candidate without a new independent mechanism and prospective diagnosis. Their observational negatives do not imply all possible routes are exhausted.\n\n## 6. Next Batch\nNo admission this cycle (budget one). Resume new design when G1 reaches terminal state or a specifically articulated independent mechanism has an executable diagnostic and matched control. See `pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-141300.md`.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
